Subject: Relax return_code validation on incoming Requests

vsomeip's is_valid_return_code() is a whitelist that drops any incoming
SOME/IP message whose return_code byte is outside {0x00..0x0A, 0x20..0x5E}.
SOME/IP defines return_code semantics only for Response/Error message
types — for Requests the byte is reserved/undefined.

TC8 §5.1.5.7 SOMEIPSRV_RPC_07/_08 verify that the DUT ignores the value
of the return_code byte on incoming Method Requests (RPC_07 sends 0xC0,
RPC_08 sends 0x01 then 0x1F). Upstream vsomeip drops the request at the
endpoint before the dispatcher sees it, so the spec assertion is
unobservable on a Linux DUT.

This patch gates the is_valid_return_code() check at both server-endpoint
call sites (UDP + TCP) on the message type: requests skip the check,
responses/errors/notifications still go through the existing whitelist.

Affects:
  implementation/endpoints/src/udp_server_endpoint_impl.cpp
  implementation/endpoints/src/tcp_server_endpoint_impl.cpp
